WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.968
-Thank you so much, New York.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.502
Oh, my God,
I'm so happy to be back.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:06.039
I've been traveling a lot
recently, which has been fun,

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.075
but it's weird, like, I've
noticed that my race changes

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.644
city to city?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.679
Like, when I'm in Chicago,
people just think that

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.947
I'm half black, half white.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:16.883
When I'm in New York, people
think that I'm Puerto Rican?

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.784
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.254
But when I'm in CVS,
everyone thinks I'm stealing.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:24.290
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.330
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.634
Which, you know,
it's really frustrating.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.836
Um...because I am.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.373
And I don't want them
to catch me.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.342
But also, like, why do you think
that I'm stealing?

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.643
I look like I'm in a brochure

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:48.114
for a very expensive
liberal arts school? So...

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.214
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:52.051
Mm. Leave me alone.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.053
[ Laughter ]
ChapStick should be free.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:57.190
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.626
My favorite articles right now
are all the articles of, like,

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.829
older people trying to come
to terms with the fact that

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.597
millennials are just poor.
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:07.900
Like the best one
I've seen is...

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.036
[ Haughty voice ] "why aren't
millennials buying diamonds?"

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:15.808
[ Laughter ]
"The industry is in peril."

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.277
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.646
And it's like one time I spent
more than $40 on groceries,

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:23.116
and my bank thought someone
stole my debit card.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.184
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:29.355
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.291
Like, I would love --
I would love to get a chain,

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.993
but first I got to stop looking
at salmon

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.296
as a high-risk investment,
you know?

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.264
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.801
There's levels to this.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.469
Kind of feel like ever since
Trump won,

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.606
everything I do is radical
just because I'm a minority.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:50.109
Like I wake up in the morning,
revolutionary.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.078
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.246
I ask the cashier for a cup
of water

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.582
but I low-key get some Sprite?
Anti-capitalist.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.884
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.019
But I feel like the election
has changed us although in ways

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.689
we're, like, just starting
to now realize.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.791
'Cause the other day,
I was on the train,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.358
and I see this, like,
mid-20s white dude,

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:11.731
like, very fit, athletic,
kind of fratty, professional,

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.300
just hit a crack pipe
and start freestyling?

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.236
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.771
And, like, that's a level I'm
trying to get at, you know?

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.172
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:23.209
Like, chasing all my dreams
at once, really.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:27.413
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.415
That's my goal. [ Chuckles ]

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.085
I can be kind of
an awkward flirt sometimes.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.419
I can have a hard time flirting,

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.488
just because people don't always
read me as queer

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.889
when they first meet me

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.692
because I've been told that
I can come across as "masc,"

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.994
and if you don't know what that
means, it's basically just gay

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:45.031
for... [ Chuckles ]
"I'm not like other girls."

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.465
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.502
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:57.209
It's like a little weird, but I
actually really like whiskey.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.979
So, I'm kind of quirky,
you know?

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.851
I'm living in L.A. right now,
which is fun.

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:07.820
I miss New York so much,
but I found a way

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.757
to make L.A. fun in that
I'm just fully trying to hook up

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.291
with Uber drivers.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.827
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.929
And like, the other day, y'all,
like, I got so close.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.565
Like I get in the car,
the guy's cute.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.066
He's like, "Oh, where you
coming from?"

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.333
And I was like, "oh, a show."

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:22.668
And he's like, "oh, what
instrument do you play?"

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.071
And I was like, "the voice."
[ Laughs ]

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.974
But I was like, "no, I do
stand-up or whatever,"

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.977
and I say, "or whatever," so he
knows that I'm humble.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:34.013
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.085
And then he goes, "oh, my God,
like, I love stand-up."

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.855
"I've actually written a couple
jokes but I'm a little nervous

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.958
to get on stage and try it."
And I was like, "oh, my God, no,

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:49.762
you seem like you have such
a...natural stage presence."

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.996
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:53.165
I was like, "here, just tell me
a joke right now,

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.501
and we can work on it
in the car together."

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.003
And he was like, "are you sure?
I don't want to, like,

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.804
waste your time." I was like,
"no, just, like, go for it."

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.205
He was like...
[ Exhales deeply ] "okay, so,

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:03.676
uh... [ Inhales deeply ]
me and my girlfriend..."

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.845
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:06.979
And I was like, "needs work.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:10.016
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.026
"Right here is fine. You can
just drop me off right now."

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.894
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.829
But ultimately though, like,
I think the hardest part

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:26.199
about traveling is that you
really just start to lose track

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.801
of how hot you are
at a certain point

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.703
'cause like it's cliché
but it's true,

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.771
that, like, a Chicago hot is
a New York cute,

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:36.142
and a New York cute
is an L.A. shunned.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.977
[ Laughter ]
Because, like, my brothers --

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:41.780
like, my, brothers are L.A.
They're both, like, tall, fit.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.317
They carry themselves
with confidence.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:48.354
I'm small, pale, I carry myself
like an inbred European Prince?

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:52.458
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.727
[ Applause ]

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.796
Like, I don't even really, like,
step when I walk.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:05:00.633
I just sort of, like, glide
everywhere that I go. You know?

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.069
But I know I'm not ugly.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.204
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.539
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:09.242
All right.
Thank you. Oh, thank you!

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.177
[ Applause ]

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.779
Like on a one to 10 scale,
I don't think that I could,

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.415
like, model,
but I could definitely

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.519
end a Republican Senator's
career. You know?

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.720
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I feel like

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.955
I'm gonna like...
All right, thank you, guys.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.725
You guys have been so much fun!
Thanks!

